Saphira Horizon branding: provenance and regeneration.

The two SVG files in this directory are TEXT (valid XML with base64
data-URI raster inside), safe for the pure-text public mirror. They
replace Horizon's default logo.svg (navbar, dark background) and
logo-splash.svg (login page, light background) at package build time.
No Horizon template is modified: the <img> references stay byte-
identical; only the pixels change.

Sources (NOT vendored — binary assets do not belong in files/):
  logo.svg:
    https://saphira.vm2.uk/images/saphira-linux-brand-icon-light-logo-320.webp
    (light variant: the navbar behind it is dark; 320x107)
  logo-splash.svg:
    ~/saphira-openstack-logo.png
    ("SaphiraLinux OpenStack" lockup, 1840x855 RGBA), scaled to
    640x297 with Pillow (thumbnail, optimize) before embedding.

Regeneration (run on a machine with Pillow):
  python3 -c "
  import base64
  def svg(data, mime, w, h, out):
      b64 = base64.b64encode(data).decode()
      open(out, 'w').write(
        '<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" '
        'xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" '
        'width=\"%d\" height=\"%d\" viewBox=\"0 0 %d %d\">'
        '<image width=\"%d\" height=\"%d\" '
        'xlink:href=\"data:%s;base64,%s\"/></svg>'
        % (w, h, w, h, w, h, mime, b64))
  svg(open('logo-navbar-320.webp','rb').read(), 'image/webp',
      320, 107, 'logo.svg')
  svg(open('logo-splash-640.png','rb').read(), 'image/png',
      640, 297, 'logo-splash.svg')
  "
  then: python3 -c "import xml.dom.minidom
  [xml.dom.minidom.parse(f) for f in ['logo.svg','logo-splash.svg']]"

Why SVG wrappers and not raw PNG/WebP: Horizon's templates reference
*.svg by name. An <img>-loaded SVG must be self-contained (external
file references are blocked), hence data URIs; serving raster bytes
under an .svg name would break on MIME mismatch. The wrapper keeps
both constraints satisfied with zero template churn.
